(Bug #31 - a text flag with no default segfaulted when the flag was not
 supplied: the slot held a literal 0 and the first read dereferenced it.
 LANGUAGE.md makes `with default` optional, so this is legal code. The
 fix gives an undefaulted text flag the same shared empty string that
 emit_type_default gives an ordinary `a text called x.` - bug #16's cure,
 which this path never received.

 Run with no arguments: outdir must read as "" and not crash.)
a flag called outdir is "-o" or "--out", it is a text.
Parse flags.
Print "text-no-default:{outdir}".
